{"name":"Rose Gold","hex":"#b76e79","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rose gold","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A gold-copper alloy used in jewelry for its reddish color.","An orange-pink color, similar to the alloy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rose_gold"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rose Gold (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Rose Gold is the debut studio album by South African singer-songwriter Shekhinah. It was released by Sony Music Entertainment Africa on October 6, 2017. Rose Gold was certified gold by the Recording Industry of South Africa on January 24, 2018 and later certified platinum on August 31, 2018. The album features guest appearances from South African rapper, Rouge, Asali and Jamali band member, Mariechan. Production is handled by David Scott, DJ Maphorisa, Mae N. Maejor, Shekhinah and Luke Goliath."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/10/Rose_Gold_%28album%29_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_Gold_(album)"},{"title":"Colored gold","blocks":[{"text":"Colored gold is any gold alloy that has a distinctive color. Pure gold is slightly reddish yellow in color, but colored gold can come in a variety of different colors by alloying it with different elements."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Ag-Au-Cu-colours-english.svg/330px-Ag-Au-Cu-colours-english.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colored_gold"},{"title":"Rose","blocks":[{"text":"A rose is either a woody perennial flowering plant of the genus Rosa, in the family Rosaceae, or the flower it bears. There are over three hundred species and tens of thousands of cultivars. The plants range in size and form, from trailing and erect shrubs to climbers up to 7 metres (23 ft) in height. Sharp prickles appear on the stems of many species. Their flowers vary in size and shape and are usually large and showy, in colours ranging from white through pinks, reds, oranges and yellows."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg/330px-Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose"},{"title":"Gold","blocks":[{"text":"Gold is a chemical element; its chemical symbol is Au and atomic number 79. In its pure form, it is a bright-metallic-yellow, dense, soft, malleable, and ductile metal. Chemically, gold is a transition metal, a group 11 element, and one of the noble metals. It is one of the least reactive chemical elements, being the second lowest in the reactivity series, with only platinum ranked as less reactive. Gold is solid under standard conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Gold-crystals.jpg/330px-Gold-crystals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/White-gold--rhodium-plated.jpg/500px-White-gold--rhodium-plated.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/White-gold--rhodium-plated.jpg/500px-White-gold--rhodium-plated.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rhodium-plated white gold wedding ring","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWhite-gold--rhodium-plated.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Rose_Gold_Diamond_Engagement_Ring.jpg/500px-Rose_Gold_Diamond_Engagement_Ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Rose_Gold_Diamond_Engagement_Ring.jpg/500px-Rose_Gold_Diamond_Engagement_Ring.jpg?utm